        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b6ff30fe-5f12-50ce-9e68-9e28020d20de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Home Rule League, Irish Parliamentary Party\n- Movements: Irish Home Rule movement\n- People: John Dunbar\n- Places: Ireland, New Ross, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland\n- Events: New Ross by-election of 1878\n- Roles: Member of Parliament\n\nFacts:\n- The Irish Home Rule movement agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League operated from 1873 to 1882 as a political party that campaigned for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League was sometimes called the Home Rule Party or the Home Rule Confederation.\n- John Dunbar was a Home Rule League politician who served as Member of Parliament for New Ross from February 1874 until his death in 1878.\n- The New Ross by-election of 1878 was fought because the incumbent Home Rule Member of Parliament, John Dunbar, died.\n- The Home Rule League was later replaced by the Irish Parliamentary Party.",
